AC1 specifies verification "via the screen's own displayed order-id text" on OrderTrackingScreen.
Live check (iPhone 17 Pro sim, phone form factor) found NO order-id text anywhere in the
OrderTrackingScreen accessibility/semantics tree (ui_list_ios after navigating to
/track-order?id=170 showed only: Back, Delivered, Delivery Partner, Delivery on the way,
Delivery partner has not been assigned yet, Need help?, Order Confirmed, Order Placed,
Order Summary, Preparing Item, Use my current location -- no "#170"/order-id string).

Code read confirms why: UserApp/lib/features/order/widgets/order_info_widget.dart:156-172
renders the '#${order.id}' Text widget ONLY inside an `if (isDesktop) [...]` branch:

    isDesktop
        ? Text('general_info'.tr, style: NearsText.subtitle)
        : NSectionHeader(title: 'order_summary'.tr),
    ...
    if (isDesktop) ...[
      Row(... Text(parcel ? 'delivery_id'.tr : 'order_id'.tr, ...), Text('#${order.id}', ...)),
      ...
    ]

On a phone (isDesktop == false, the form factor AC1's "device"/live-demo implies), that whole
block is skipped, so the mobile OrderTrackingScreen never displays the order id as text at all.
This is PRE-EXISTING (order_info_widget.dart is untouched by NEARS-2501's diff) and unrelated
to this ticket's fix -- filed as a regression_bug, does not block this ticket's verdict on its
own, but it means AC1's literal verification method is unavailable on mobile; the underlying
no-misroute behavior was instead verified via OrderController.trackModel.id state + the real
backend network round trip for the exact requested order id (see ac1-source-discriminator.log).
